prompt:
Create ONE professional FULL-BODY 24-frame transparent animation sprite atlas of the dragon girl in REFERENCE1, moving in the specific poses in REFERENCE2. This is the COMPLETE PAINTED CHARACTER in every cell, never separate body parts or a skeleton.
REFERENCE1 (single girl) is the ONLY identity, proportions, palette, line/shading style and clothing design. Keep her EXACT little face/eyes, compact short CHIBI body and legs, silver-white long curls, violet eyes, paired segmented white horns, curved ahoge, pointed ears, white flower head ornament, pale lavender bat wings and thick curled white scaled tail. Same detailed white OFF-SHOULDER ornate fitted dress and delicate silver front clasp, waist flower/ribbons, long layered ruffled sides with SHORT OPEN FRONT showing the legs, leg strap and white shoes. No redesign, no simplified outfit, no elongated legs/torso, no larger skull or eyes.
REFERENCE2 (red/blue stick figure guide) is ONLY the EXACT24 consecutive jogging POSES and cell placement. Render her complete natural limbs underneath the SAME unchanged garment, at those24 poses. Red leg and arm are NEAR SIDE, blue are FAR SIDE, same identities across all frames. Do not draw diagram bones, joints, red/blue colors, guide numbers, frame borders, ground lines or arrows in the final. Use guide to get actual distinct leg phases rather than one generic running pose.
Layout EXACT6 equal columns by4 equal rows, 24 cells, row-major. Orthographic consistent LEFT-facing3/4 profile, nose points SCREEN LEFT, fixed camera and zoom; head/torso position fixed within each cell. Keep sufficient transparent padding around all horns, ahoge, wings, tail and shoes, no neighbor overlap or clipping. All24 character models have identical overall scale, head size, short body proportions and clothing/hair volume. Final background truly alpha-zero transparent, no colored/gradient background, ground, shadow, text, grid or checkerboard.
Action is ONE complete gentle SLOW JOG cycle across24 frames, about1.8seconds, not four repeated short cycles. Follow each guide pose carefully:
1-6 NEAR leg supports while FAR leg folds and swings forward, near-side arm swinging backward and far-side arm forward;
7-11 FAR leg descends into forward contact while NEAR leg leaves support;
12 brief BOTH-FEET airborne transition (tiny clearance, gentle);
13-18 FAR leg now supports, NEAR knee lifts and NEAR foot swings forward; arms have reversed (near arm forward, far arm backward);
19-23 NEAR foot comes forward toward contact while FAR leg leaves support;
24 brief both-feet airborne before frame1 contact.
The near foot must visibly be in front in one half-cycle and behind in the other, and the far leg does the opposite. Do not leave the same leg permanently forward or merely shuffle the toes. Include passing, support, lift and forward reach. Elbows/wrists move continuously, never teleport a hand at a row boundary.
Keep body bob extremely small (about1-2 pixels at this sprite scale), slight forward lean3degrees only, no head wobble or independent head-size changes. Eyes both open and same face all24 frames; no wink or new expression. Tiny continuous sleeve, tail and hair follow-through. Row boundaries are consecutive motion frames, not a new pose/viewpoint/layout. Make24→1 a smooth continuation. Clean antialiased edges, no white/colored dust islands.
